= Negotiations, Pt. 1

Following Staal's resignation, DuFour personally commissioned Goodryke to explore the formation of a new cabinet. The man responsible for poisoning the President’s mind against Staal is now to demand the appointment of [+ royalist_chancellor +] as chancellor, while refusing the office for himself.

Prior to this, Goodryke met with <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leaders such as Gorrick and Frask at Ribbentrop’s villa, where they agreed on a strategy to convince DuFour that [+ royalist_chancellor +] would lead a "nationalist front" cabinet composed mostly of conservatives. This plan also won over Oskar, who, during a tea meeting with Ribbentrop, was persuaded to support the idea. To achieve this, the group must now win Mallin’s backing.

However, the collapse of the Harzburg Front, Mallin's distrust of [+ royalist_chancellor +], and the latter's personality make this a difficult task. The schemers therefore turn to negotiations with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>, hoping to pressure Mallin to go alone with them.

- @nazi_2

@nazi_2
title: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> and the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>?] are sounded out for cabinet posts.

Franz Selden of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>, a staunch opponent of Staal’s efforts to bring his paramilitary under state control, quickly succumbed to the promise of a cabinet post. His decision is announced during negotiations with Mallin, putting the latter at a disadvantage and increasing the pressure on him to follow suit.

However, [+ royalist_leader +] overplayed his hand, using this advantage to demand that a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> be appointed to the national[? if heartland_leader == "Staal":&nbsp;and Heartland?] Interior ministries[? if heartland_leader == "Staal":, with the Heartland one being especially important due to its direct control over the police?]. [? if heartland_leader == "Staal": Mallin balked at [+ royalist_leader +]’s demands, insisting that the Heartland Interior Ministry go to a non-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span>, and that the Chancellery chief of staff and cabinet spokesman come from his own party. ?][? if heartland_leader != "Staal": Mallin was largely amenable to [+ royalist_leader +]’s demands, but now insists that the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> withdraw their claim to the Interior Ministry, and that the Chancellery chief of staff and cabinet spokesman come from his party. ?]

[? if heartland_leader == "Staal": Furious at being blocked, [+ royalist_leader +] broke off negotiations, refused to meet Goodryke, and threatened to return to Munich. Only with difficulty did Gorrick and Ribbentrop persuade him to remain in Axton. Goodryke, desperate to keep talks alive, agreed to support [+ royalist_leader +]’s demands for both interior ministries and the freedom to choose Chancellery personnel—on the condition that he himself would oversee the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> Interior Minister of Heartland as Minister-President. ?][? if heartland_leader != "Staal": Furious at being blocked, [+ royalist_leader +] broke off negotiations, refused to meet Goodryke, and threatened to return to Munich. Only with difficulty did Gorrick and Ribbentrop persuade him to remain in Axton. Goodryke, desperate to keep talks alive, agreed to support [+ royalist_leader +]’s demands for the Interior Ministry and the freedom to appoint Chancellery personnel. Whether Mallin will yield on the issue remains unclear. ?]

- @nazi_3
- @nazi_4

@nazi_3
title: A furious [+ royalist_leader +] challenges Goodryke's claim on Heartland!
subtitle: He threatens to break off negotiations for good.
view-if: heartland_leader == "Staal"

[+ royalist_leader +], already incensed by Mallin, now objects to Goodryke’s demand to become Minister-President of Heartland. Goodryke urges Ribbentrop and Gorrick to convince [+ royalist_leader +] to give up the issue, and once again, they manage to calm him with great difficulty.

[+ royalist_leader +] agrees to think over the Heartland question overnight and meet Goodryke again the following morning.

- @nazi_5

@nazi_4
title: Negotiations will continue nonetheless.
view-if: heartland_leader != "Staal"

[+ royalist_leader +], though personally irritated by the concessions he has been forced to make, agrees—under the influence of Gorrick and Ribbentrop—to meet with Goodryke once again in the morning.

- @nazi_5_alt

@nazi_5
title: Goodryke sets out to break Mallin's resistance.

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> have repeated their demand for both interior ministries, stalling progress with Mallin. Seeking compromise, Goodryke expresses support for Mallin's request to control the ministries of economics and agriculture in both the Commonwealth and Heartland. Although troubled by the prospect of a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span>-controlled Heartland police force, Mallin is not yet ready to walk away from his first real chance at power.

- @nazi_6

@nazi_5_alt
title: Goodryke sets out to break Mallin's resistance.

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> have repeated their demand for the interior ministry, stalling progress with Mallin. In an effort to break the impasse, Goodryke voices support for Mallin’s claim to the Ministries of Economics and Agriculture—granting him significant influence over national economic policy. Though deeply uneasy about the prospect of a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span>-dominated police force, Mallin is not yet willing to abandon his first real shot at power, and reluctantly agrees to continue negotiations.

- @nazi_6

@nazi_6
title: What about the conservative elites, the ones in Staal's cabinet? Will they remain in office?
on-arrival: dufour_gallax_r += 1

The members of Staal’s cabinet—many of whom followed him after Goodryke’s dismissal—remain deeply skeptical of a [+ royalist_chancellor +] chancellorship, given their ties to elite conservative circles. To ease their concerns, Goodryke hints that DuFour is already open to appointing [+ royalist_chancellor +], and that he would be the fallback choice should the effort fail.

Moreover, Staal’s warnings that Goodryke’s return would lead to civil war only further drive his ministers to back [+ royalist_chancellor +] over Goodryke.

- @nazi_7

@nazi_7
title: The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> offers to negotiate to back a parliamentary [+ royalist_chancellor +] cabinet.
subtitle: A wrench in Goodryke's plans!

Fritz Schäffer, chairman of the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span>, approaches [+ royalist_leader +] and Goodryke, announcing that the two [? if not stegerwald_path: Catholic?][? if stegerwald_path: Christian?] parties would be willing to participate in a parliamentary cabinet headed by [+ royalist_chancellor +]. This arrangement would bar Goodryke’s return and give them the power to collapse the government at any time.

Though this would be the only realistic chance for DuFour to appoint [+ royalist_chancellor +], the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leader knows too well the risks of parliamentary dependency and continues to push for a presidential cabinet. Goodryke is also well aware that if the [? if not stegerwald_path: Catholic?][? if stegerwald_path: Christian?] parties formally support a parliamentary route, DuFour might act on their offer and reject [+ royalist_chancellor +] if he refuses to accept it. Furthermore, a deal between Mallin and the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> remains highly improbable.

To stall this threat, Goodryke deliberately withholds the proposal from DuFour, while the [? if not stegerwald_path: Catholic?][? if stegerwald_path: Christian?] parties refrain from announcing their position publicly as to not compromise negotiations.

The day ends with DuFour’s resistance wearing down. Goodryke has refused the chancellorship. Only [+ royalist_chancellor +] remains.